     1,
     "<br><br>On Thursday, May 16, 2013 6:46:26 PM UTC+1, Sam wrote:<div><br>&lt;snip&gt;<br> <br></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><pre style=\"word-wrap:break-word;width:744px\"><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px\">curl <a href=\"http://nodejs.org/dist/node-latest.tar.gz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://nodejs.org/dist/node-latest.tar.gz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2CKVl9XXFLL_UEEJND-xvV\">http://nodejs.org/dist/node-latest.tar.gz</a> | tar xz --strip-components<span style=\"font-weight:bold\">=</span>1   </div><div style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Consolas,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,Courier,monospace;font-size:12px;line-height:16px\"><br></div><div><font size=\"2\" color=\"#000000\" face=\"Consolas, Liberation Mono, Courier, monospace\"><span style=\"line-height:16px\"><b style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">Got this issue when executed the above command - &gt; curl: (6) Couldn&#39;t resolve host &#39;<a href=\"http://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://nodejs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZtmAw5fxwqSlTTmlDCQ4Y\">nodejs.org</a>&#39;</b></span></font></div></pre></div></blockquote>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div><br>This is a network or DNS resolution problem - are you sure your system is connected to the network with Internet access? If it is, then try typing this command:<br><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><br>host <a href=\"http://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://nodejs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZtmAw5fxwqSlTTmlDCQ4Y\">nodejs.org</a><br><br></div>and you should see something like this:<br><br><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><a href=\"http://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://nodejs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZtmAw5fxwqSlTTmlDCQ4Y\">nodejs.org</a> has address 165.225.133.150<br></div><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><a href=\"http://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://nodejs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZtmAw5fxwqSlTTmlDCQ4Y\">nodejs.org</a> mail is handled by 10 <a href=\"http://mail.nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mail.nodejs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw16NWhgup5OOEFi4Uq2eNSK\">mail.nodejs.org</a>.<br><br></div>If this does not work or you receive an error message, maybe your /etc/resolv.conf file is missing or incorrectly configured. If it&#39;s missing, just create one containing the line:<br><br><div style=\"margin-left:40px\">nameserver 8.8.8.8<br><br></div>and this should work. If the file is present, try changing it to read &#39;nameserver 8.8.8.8&#39; as described above. If having done this you still can&#39;t resolve the IP address for <a href=\"http://nodejs.org\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://nodejs.org&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792408960555000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3ZtmAw5fxwqSlTTmlDCQ4Y\">nodejs.org</a> then perhaps your /etc/nsswitch.conf is incorrect but this is not very common.<br><br>Hope this helps with this part of the installation...<br><br></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
